88 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 61 0 R
/T (Electricity consumption is an important quantity to observe in homes, laboratories and industrial environments. A conventional meter generally provides a reading that must be checked at the meter itself. A smart electronic monitoring arrangement can make electrical readings easier to observe by processing sensor information and showing it on a digital display.)
/E (Electricity consumption is an important quantity to observe in homes, laboratories and industrial environments. A conventional meter generally provides a reading that must be checked at the meter itself. A smart electronic monitoring arrangement can make electrical readings easier to observe by processing sensor information and showing it on a digital display.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
89 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 61 0 R
/T (In this project, a voltage sensor and a current sensor are used to detect the electrical parameters. Their outputs are analog signals. The ESP32 reads these signals through its analog-to-digital converter \(ADC\), processes the resulting digital values and sends information to the LCD using an I2C interface. The display provides a convenient visual output for the measured parameters. The project is educational in nature. It helps connect the theoretical concepts of sensors, ADC, microcontrollers and serial communication with a working electronic-system design.)
/E (In this project, a voltage sensor and a current sensor are used to detect the electrical parameters. Their outputs are analog signals. The ESP32 reads these signals through its analog-to-digital converter \(ADC\), processes the resulting digital values and sends information to the LCD using an I2C interface. The display provides a convenient visual output for the measured parameters. The project is educational in nature. It helps connect the theoretical concepts of sensors, ADC, microcontrollers and serial communication with a working electronic-system design.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
