/P 70 0 R
/E (The Smart Electric Meter project demonstrates the practical use of digital electronics in electrical measurement. It combines voltage and current sensors, analog-to-digital conversion, a microcontroller and LCD interfacing to create a basic energy-monitoring arrangement.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
213 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 70 0 R
/E (The voltage and current sensors detect electrical parameters and provide analog signals. The ESP32 ADC converts these signals into digital values. The microcontroller processes the values, and the processed information is transferred to the LCD through the I2C interface. The LCD then displays the measured parameters.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
