499 0 obj
<<
/Title (Electricity consumption is an important quantity to observe in homes, laboratories and industrial environments. A conventional meter generally provides a reading that must be checked at the meter itself. A smart electronic monitoring arrangement can make electrical readings easier to observe by processing sensor information and showing it on a digital display.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 438 0 R
/Next 500 0 R
>>
endobj
500 0 obj
<<
/Title (In this project, a voltage sensor and a current sensor are used to detect the electrical parameters. Their outputs are analog signals. The ESP32 reads these signals through its analog-to-digital converter \(ADC\), processes the resulting digital values and sends information to the LCD using an I2C interface. The display provides a convenient visual output for the measured parameters. The project is educational in nature. It helps connect the theoretical concepts of sensors, ADC, microcontrollers and serial communication with a working electronic-system design.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 438 0 R
/Prev 499 0 R
>>
endobj
